{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.RivinConcavity","lean:module:QOU.Knot.LobNearZero","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LobachevskyMaximum"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.lob_sum_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.lob_sum_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobMonotonicity.lean#L182-L209","doc":"**The ideal-tetrahedron Λ-sum is nonnegative.**\n\n`α, β, γ > 0` summing to `π`.  At most one exceeds `π/2`; if one does, fold it\nwith `Lob_pi_sub` and apply subadditivity to the other two, whose sum is then\n`≤ π/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.Lob_add_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.Lob_add_le","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobMonotonicity.lean#L152-L179","doc":"**`Λ` is subadditive on `[0, π/2]`**: concave with `Λ 0 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.Lob_nonneg_of_le_pi_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.Lob_nonneg_of_le_pi_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobMonotonicity.lean#L128-L149","doc":"**`Λ ≥ 0` on `[0, π/2]`** — a concave function vanishing at both endpoints\nis nonnegative between them, and `Λ 0 = Λ(π/2) = 0`.\n\nDerived here rather than imported: the corpus's `Lob_nonneg_of_lt_pi_div_two`\nlives in `QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume` (`OrthoschemeWedgePair`), whose cone\nis the orthoscheme/measure-theory development — far heavier than this one line\nneeds, and this version also covers the endpoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.concaveOn_Lob","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.concaveOn_Lob","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobMonotonicity.lean#L106-L124","doc":"**`Λ` is concave on `[0, π/2]`** — from `Λ'' = −cot < 0` on the interior,\nwhich the corpus already proves (`deriv_deriv_Lob_neg`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.Lob_pi_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.Lob_pi_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobMonotonicity.lean#L99-L103","doc":"`Λ(π/2) = 0`, since `Cl₂(π) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.Lob_sub_Lob_add_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.Lob_sub_Lob_add_pos","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobMonotonicity.lean#L74-L82","doc":"The form the chord argument consumes: folding an obtuse angle with\n`Lob_pi_sub` turns the sum into a difference, and this makes it positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.strictAntiOn_Lob","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.strictAntiOn_Lob","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobMonotonicity.lean#L62-L72","doc":"**`Λ` is strictly decreasing on `[π/6, 5π/6]`.**\n\nThis is the fact `qou-52ch`'s chord argument needs, and it is a statement about\nthe SIGN of `Λ′`, never about a value of `Λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.deriv_Lob_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.deriv_Lob_neg","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobMonotonicity.lean#L52-L60","doc":"`Λ′(t) < 0` on `(π/6, 5π/6)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.one_lt_two_mul_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity.one_lt_two_mul_sin","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobMonotonicity.lean#L34-L50","doc":"`2 sin t > 1` on `(π/6, 5π/6)` — the exact locus where `Λ′ < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}